course: dictionary
lesson: 3673
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have several meanings, and context tells you which one is meant. The word fix can mean repair, attach, decide or trouble. «Four coders who each fix 12 bugs a day fix 4 × 12 = 48 bugs a day.» Here fix means to repair or correct, because the bugs are mistakes that get put right. Try your meaning in the sentence: fix bugs, or repair bugs, both make sense.
explain: Now read this: «Owning up and asking for help with the part you didn't understand is the real fix for cheating in learning.» Here a fix is a solution to a problem. Ask yourself: what word would fit? The answer is solution, and it makes sense in the sentence.
explain: Sometimes the clue is in the words next to fix. «Fixed costs are bills that come every month, like rent.» The word fixed means the bills do not change. A fixed number stays the same, so fixed here means it does not change.
fact: Fix is a verb (fix, fixes, fixed, fixing) and it can also be a noun (a fix, fixes).
fact: «Fix» can mean to repair something so it works again, such as a broken bike or tap.
fact: «Fix» can mean to attach something firmly in place, such as a shelf to the wall.
fact: «Fixed» means does not change, as in «fixed costs» like rent.
fact: Being in a fix means being in trouble, and a quick fix is a fast solution to a problem.
exercise: «Four coders who each fix 12 bugs a day fix 4 × 12 = 48 bugs a day.» What does fix mean here? | *To repair or correct | To decide on a date | To attach firmly to a wall | To make a meal
exercise: «Fixed costs are bills that come every month, like rent.» What does fixed mean here? | Broken | Very fast | Painted | *Does not change
exercise: Dad says «I am in a fix.» What does being in a fix mean? | Having a fixed price | *Being in trouble | Being very fit and strong | Being at the workshop
test: «Owning up is the real fix for cheating in learning.» Here fix means | A shelf fixed to a wall | A broken toy | *A solution to a problem | A date that has been decided
test: A robot follows its steps exactly; a mistake in the steps is called a bug, and finding and fixing it is called debugging. What is debugging? | *Finding and repairing a mistake in a robot's steps | Fixing a robot to the floor | Turning the robot off for the day | Writing new steps for a robot to follow
exam: Which phrase uses fix to mean attach something firmly in place? | Fix a puncture on the bike | *Fix a shelf to the wall | Fix a date for the trip | Fix a meal for the family
